{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1273286-trinity-continuum-core-errata","id":1273286,"title":"Trinity Continuum core errata","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-12-07T11:14:49-08:00","id":1273286,"title":"Trinity Continuum core errata","content":"Please list your errata for the <b>Trinity Continuum</b> core rulebook here.<ul><li>Please address only typos, layout glitches, misplaced elements, and similar errors. If it's merely a matter where you'd have phrased something differently, that's not errata, and should go in a different thread.</li> <li>Please confine comments to posting errata. Discussion should also go elsewhere.</li> <li>Missing art and Page XXs are known quantities and are not being called out at this time. There's no need to list them here.</li> </ul><br /> Thank you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-07T12:08:44-08:00","id":1273294,"title":"","content":"Layout issue on page 127 wording is off on top of vehicle Chart.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6424-fuzzykuma","name":"Fuzzykuma","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6424_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"178"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-07T12:48:54-08:00","id":1273298,"title":"","content":"Shockwave tag is referred to on p117 and p118, highlighted as something very important to running Vehicle combat effectively.<br /> <br /> No Shockwave tag exists.<br /> <br /> It could just be the name that is wrong on p117-118, but I have not been able to easily identify another tag that fits the description.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6463-proteus_est","name":"Proteus_Est","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-07T12:59:07-08:00","id":1273300,"title":"","content":"I'm credited as Craig Oxbow (not Oxbrow) on pages 2 and 3.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Craig Oxbrow<br /> <b>The Trinity Continuum</b> freelancer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/221-craig-oxbrow","name":"Craig Oxbrow","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar221_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-07T13:41:56-08:00","id":1273309,"title":"","content":"Second Path named both Profession and Role;<br /> <br /> Page 36 - 2nd paragraph<br /> <br /> &quot;In Trinity Continuum each character has three Paths: Origin, <b>Profession</b>, and Society&quot;<br /> <br /> Page 36 - 4th paragraph<br /> <br /> &quot;The <b>Role </b>Path is the character\u2019s occupation &quot;<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23807-greenozzy","name":"Greenozzy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23807_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-07T13:55:15-08:00","id":1273311,"title":"","content":"Should things like references to the Red and Black pools still being in the text be part of this errata thread or just layout and spelling issues?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23807-greenozzy","name":"Greenozzy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23807_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-07T14:06:44-08:00","id":1273314,"title":"","content":"Page 155 - LIFE-THREATENING ACCIDENT does not have the blue box around it like the other Moment of Inspiration headers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23807-greenozzy","name":"Greenozzy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23807_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-07T14:06:54-08:00","id":1273315,"title":"","content":"<b>Forceful Martial Arts \u2022\u2022: Deadly Strike</b> (p63) refers to the Slow tag. No such Tag appears to exist.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>---------------------------------------------<br /> Supporter of Spirits getting full playable splat design come Exalted 3E.<br /> Refugee from the 3rd Great Edition Wars of D&amp;D. <br /> oWoD Latecomer, Exalted Optimist, Scion ST, Trinity Curious","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/955-yue-ryong","name":"Yue Ryong","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar955_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"147"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-07T14:09:11-08:00","id":1273316,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Greenozzy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1273286-trinity-continuum-core-errata?p=1273311#post1273311\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Should things like references to the Red and Black pools still being in the text be part of this errata thread or just layout and spelling issues?</div> </div> </div> </div>Those can be included here, yes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-07T14:12:55-08:00","id":1273317,"title":"","content":"p.39 Experience reward table uses a column header of Experience Cost<br /> p.39 The second Experience table (with what it costs to improve things) lists Adding a dot in a new or existing Path as costing 18 experience while pg 41 under Advancement with Paths says 'Each dot in a Path costs five points of Experience'.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1039-brennanhawkwood","name":"Brennanhawkwood","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"56"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-07T14:23:28-08:00","id":1273320,"title":"","content":"The entirety of Chapter 7: Gifts is riddled with P.XX references.<br /> P.79 has a p.XX reference for &quot;Moving and Maneuvering&quot;.<br /> <br /> Edit: scratch that. There are tons of P. XX references throughout the book. From pages 37 to 212.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4881,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4881-veros","user":"Veros","date":". 12-07-2018, 05:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4881-veros","name":"Veros","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-07T14:29:34-08:00","id":1273322,"title":"","content":"p. 39: Experience is referred to as being spent after an 'Arc', which I suspect is meant to be 'Chronicle'.<br /> <br /> Character Sheet has space only for your starting three paths, rather than the five you can potentially move into.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>---------------------------------------------<br /> Supporter of Spirits getting full playable splat design come Exalted 3E.<br /> Refugee from the 3rd Great Edition Wars of D&amp;D. <br /> oWoD Latecomer, Exalted Optimist, Scion ST, Trinity Curious","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/955-yue-ryong","name":"Yue Ryong","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar955_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"147"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-07T14:39:11-08:00","id":1273324,"title":"","content":"Refrences to Red Pool:<br /> Pg 97 - Jinxed<br /> Pg 120 - Turning Points - 4th paragraph<br /> <br /> Refrences to Black Pool:<br /> Pg 73 - Momentum - 2nd paragraph<br /> <br /> <br /> Footer issues:<br /> It looks like some footers that have multiple sections on them list both section names and others don't. Not certain if this is because there is a difference between types of Sections or not. There is not visible difference.<br /> Example: Pg 35 has both section names (Step One: Concepts|Step Two: Paths). Pg 79 has both The Three Areas of Action and Action-Adventure on the pages but the footer only lists Action-Adventure<br /> <br /> Some footers have multiple section names continue from one footer to the next while others only list the most recent section name<br /> Example: Pg 149 lists both section names (Who Are Talents?|Inspiration). Pg 151 lists just Inspiration header from pg 149. But page 153 lists both headers (Paths|Creating Talents) and this carries over to the footer on page 155, unlike the prior example.<br /> <br /> Page 53 footer should be Skills (Attributes start on page 54)<br /> Page 141, 143, 147 footer still shows Storyguide Characters|Antagonists even though this section ended on pg 139<br /> Page 187 footer shows What Is A Storyguide (found on pg 129) but sections listed on page are What Are Gifts? and What Kinds Of Gifts Are There?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23807,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23807-greenozzy","user":"Greenozzy","date":". 12-07-2018, 05:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23807-greenozzy","name":"Greenozzy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23807_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-07T14:46:44-08:00","id":1273327,"title":"","content":"The Inflict Damage stunt for Close Combat is (Armor) successes, whereas for Ranged and Thrown it\u2019s (1 + Armor). In the Kickstarter preview these were all the same (1 + Armor). Is this a deliberate change or an errata point?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-07T14:57:03-08:00","id":1273332,"title":"","content":"Under Inspirational Media (pg 16) the titles for Movies, Television Shows, and Games are listed in italics. Under Books and Comics the titles are bolded. Not sure if that is a style choice or a mistake so I thought I would point it out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23807-greenozzy","name":"Greenozzy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23807_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-07T15:00:16-08:00","id":1273334,"title":"","content":"Pg 32. Hand written text of the note overlaps on top of the paperclip.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23807,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23807-greenozzy","user":"Greenozzy","date":". 12-07-2018, 06:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23807-greenozzy","name":"Greenozzy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23807_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-07T15:11:20-08:00","id":1273337,"title":"","content":"Page 106 - Unconscious condition name does not have the blue background box like other conditions.<br /> <br /> Page 108 - Special Environments - Underwater section title has a different font size from Gravity section title","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23807,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23807-greenozzy","user":"Greenozzy","date":". 12-07-2018, 06:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23807-greenozzy","name":"Greenozzy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23807_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-07T15:29:14-08:00","id":1273339,"title":"","content":"Page 124- the text says ambushing someone is a Agility+Dexterity roll. Since Agility is not a skill what should the roll be?<br /> <br /> Page 105-Broken leg says it increases the difficulty of all Agility actions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/565-therian","name":"Therian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar565_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-07T15:36:44-08:00","id":1273341,"title":"","content":"p.17 Psi: contains the line<br /> &quot;Psi is rated 1-7, but only proxies can have Psi ratings above 5.&quot;<br /> This is inconsistent with the Aeon manuscript which allows any psion to eventually reach psi levels above 5. If this is not a deliberate change, suggest removing this line of text.<br /> p.18-33 angled &quot;articles&quot; are not rendered properly. The text jumps at angles inconsistent with the the angle of the graphical article page. See the word &quot;rife&quot; in the first line on p.18 for an example. the ife are consistent with each other but not with the r. Also the word superheroes is at multiple levels and is specifically jarring.<br /> Magnets/pins also cover parts of the text.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24507,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24507-baladain","user":"Baladain","date":". 12-07-2018, 06:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24507-baladain","name":"Baladain","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-07T17:41:56-08:00","id":1273354,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\">PG 74: Under the Scales and Tier Chart, I noted Abberants are listed as Scale 5, and Novas were at Scale 4. I'm trying to see if this was intentional, as some Abberants figured out Chrysalis early on, as opposed to some of the more 'stable' Novas (I use this term loosely. I'm looking at you Pax).</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:times new roman\">PG 78: Under Example Complex Actions: Sequencing DNA requires less Milestones than Hacking a Secure Network. I am now scared of these Secure Networks. We talking Quantum-Bit cores here?</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:Mercury Text G2, serif\">PG 80: Under Range: multiple spaces between the words \u201cEach range possesses the following characteristics.\u201d </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13091,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13091-thewanderingjewels","user":"TheWanderingJewels","date":". 12-07-2018, 09:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13091-thewanderingjewels","name":"TheWanderingJewels","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13091_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-07T18:06:04-08:00","id":1273358,"title":"","content":"p61: Big Hearted Edge implies a maximum number of Bonds that you maintain at once. Bond section does not readily indicate such a limit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>---------------------------------------------<br /> Supporter of Spirits getting full playable splat design come Exalted 3E.<br /> Refugee from the 3rd Great Edition Wars of D&amp;D. <br /> oWoD Latecomer, Exalted Optimist, Scion ST, Trinity Curious","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/955-yue-ryong","name":"Yue Ryong","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar955_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"147"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-07T18:31:42-08:00","id":1273363,"title":"","content":"Leif Jones is not credited in the artists section of the credits page (page 2)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23566-jake-ekiss","name":"Jake Ekiss","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-07T18:58:54-08:00","id":1273368,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Veros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1273286-trinity-continuum-core-errata?p=1273320#post1273320\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The entirety of Chapter 7: Gifts is riddled with P.XX references.<br /> P.79 has a p.XX reference for &quot;Moving and Maneuvering&quot;.<br /> <br /> Edit: scratch that. There are tons of P. XX references throughout the book. From pages 37 to 212.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> As the first post in the thread states: &quot;<i>Missing art and Page XXs are known quantities and are not being called out at this time. There's no need to list them here.</i>&quot; Thank you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-07T20:57:49-08:00","id":1273383,"title":"","content":"Page 15: Aeon isn't bolded, while Aberrant and Adventure! are.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-07T21:51:58-08:00","id":1273391,"title":"","content":"p. 73: &quot;instead a new avenue (and often more difficult) avenue opens up.&quot; Ditch the first 'avenue.'","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-07T23:37:57-08:00","id":1273399,"title":"","content":"The \u201cManeuverable\u2019 tag is missing its formatting box. P.126","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-08T06:04:26-08:00","id":1273423,"title":"","content":"p67 - The Respected Authority Edge both lists 'Appropriate Skill \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022' as a Prerequisite and 'At least four dots in an appropriate Skill are necessary for this trait to make sense.' in the Drawbacks. Presumably one of these is redundant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>---------------------------------------------<br /> Supporter of Spirits getting full playable splat design come Exalted 3E.<br /> Refugee from the 3rd Great Edition Wars of D&amp;D. <br /> oWoD Latecomer, Exalted Optimist, Scion ST, Trinity Curious","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/955-yue-ryong","name":"Yue Ryong","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar955_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"147"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-08T09:33:06-08:00","id":1273452,"title":"","content":"p. 45 Skill Tricks<br /> Characters begin game with one Skill Trick in a Skill rated 3 or higher.<br /> Should read:<br /> Characters begin <b>the</b> game with one Skill Trick in a Skill rated 3 or higher.<br /> <br /> p. 46 Athletics - Mighty Lifter<br /> <b>You\u2019re your</b> character is attempting to lift or push something,<br /> should read:<br /> <b>Your</b> character is attempting to lift or push something,<br /> <br /> p. 47 Close Combat - Deadly Strike (clash range reference)<br /> Whenever the character engages in a mixed action in combat at <b>clash</b> range<br /> Should read:<br /> Whenever the character engages in a mixed action in combat at <b>close</b> range<br /> <br /> p. 47 Close Combat - Sucker Punch (clash range reference)<br /> Additionally, the player may spend a Momentum to add the character\u2019s Close Combat Skill to his initiative tick rating if he is in <b>clash</b> range of an opponent.<br /> should read:<br /> Additionally, the player may spend a Momentum to add the character\u2019s Close Combat Skill to his initiative tick rating if he is in <b>close</b> range of an opponent.<br /> <br /> p. 49 Enigmas - Instant Solution<br /> It isn\u2019t easy, but once you know the trick, you can solve <b>in</b> every time.<br /> Should read:<br /> It isn\u2019t easy, but once you know the trick, you can solve <b>it</b> every time.<br /> <br /> p. 52 Pilot - I Can Figure it Out<br /> Spend 1 Momentum to allow the character to Pilot any vehicle for one scene, even if that vehicle normally requires a Specialty that the character does not possess.<br /> This does not appear consistent with the use of Specialties in this system. Should this read &quot;special training&quot; instead of Specialty. I'm assuming the capitalization of Specialty means it is specifically referring to the Skill Specialty mechanic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24507-baladain","name":"Baladain","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-08T09:42:28-08:00","id":1273454,"title":"","content":"Outdated Range references:<br /> p. 47 Deadly Strike: Whenever the character engages in a mixed action in combat at <b>clash</b> range<br /> p.48 Sucker Punch: tick rating if he is in <b>clash</b> range<br /> p.80 Maneuvering: Over unexceptional terrain, characters can move between <b>near</b> and <b>clash</b> range<br /> p. 81 Sprinting: Sprinting is an extra burst of speed and works well as part of a mixed action to \u201crun and gun,\u201d or to move from <b>near</b> to <b>far</b> or beyond.<br /> p.122 Gas: This attack produces a gas cloud that affects everyone within <b>clash</b> range<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24507-baladain","name":"Baladain","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-08T12:00:31-08:00","id":1273474,"title":"","content":"Wording on p45 halfway implies Skill Tricks are automatic at 3/4/5 dots. Possible clarification needed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>---------------------------------------------<br /> Supporter of Spirits getting full playable splat design come Exalted 3E.<br /> Refugee from the 3rd Great Edition Wars of D&amp;D. <br /> oWoD Latecomer, Exalted Optimist, Scion ST, Trinity Curious","edited":{"userid":955,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/955-yue-ryong","user":"Yue Ryong","date":". 12-08-2018, 03:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/955-yue-ryong","name":"Yue Ryong","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar955_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"147"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-08T12:54:49-08:00","id":1273481,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yue Ryong</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1273286-trinity-continuum-core-errata?p=1273474#post1273474\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wording on p45 halfway implies Skill Tricks are automatic at 3/4/5 dots. Possible clarification needed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Specifically, &quot;When you reach level 3 in a Skill, you <b>can choose</b> one Skill Trick for that Skill. As your character advances in the Skill, you <b>can choose</b> an additional Skill Trick for each Dot above 3 as well.&quot;<br /> &quot;can choose&quot; should be replaced with &quot;can purchase&quot;<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24507-baladain","name":"Baladain","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-08T14:12:39-08:00","id":1273492,"title":"","content":"Bookmarking Issue: Major Allegiances are placed beneath Example CharGen, rather than their own category.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>---------------------------------------------<br /> Supporter of Spirits getting full playable splat design come Exalted 3E.<br /> Refugee from the 3rd Great Edition Wars of D&amp;D. <br /> oWoD Latecomer, Exalted Optimist, Scion ST, Trinity Curious","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/955-yue-ryong","name":"Yue Ryong","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar955_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"147"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-08T14:25:26-08:00","id":1273495,"title":"","content":"p.57 Edges - tense mismatch<br /> even to be wealthy, famous and <b>has</b> a dozen assistants at her beck and call.<br /> should read<br /> <b>have</b> a dozen assistants.<br /> <br /> p.60 Fast Draw<br /> so that she can draw from its holster<br /> should read:<br /> so that she can draw <b>it</b> from its holster<br /> <br /> p.60 Ms. Fix It.<br /> (For example, a character with two dots in Close Combat could add 2 Enhancement to a Technology + Intellect roll when fixing a blast pistol.)<br /> Seems like this should use Aim instead of Close Combat for a firearm.<br /> <br /> p.63 Forceful Martial Arts<br /> single type<br /> of hand to hand weapon, like chain weapons, <b>cubs (should be clubs)</b><br /> Deadly Strike refers to the <b>Slow</b> tag, which does not appear to be listed.<br /> &quot;but must also add the Slow tag to the weapon whenever she <b>uses for this attack</b>.&quot;<br /> Unsure of intent of this clause. Perhaps &quot;uses this attack&quot; is the intended phrasing?<br /> <br /> p. 64 Precise Martial Arts<br /> Defensive Movement<br /> If the attack<br /> is designed to grapple, then this maneuver instead increases the Difficulty of the attack by <b>two</b>.<br /> two should be replaced by 2, as fixed values in this section are designated with numerals.<br /> <br /> p.64 Sniper<br /> Dead Calm - &quot;Double the Enhancement your character gains from taking the time to carefully aim an attack.&quot;<br /> Careful Aim does not seem to exist in the combat section. How is this defined?<br /> Precision Shooting - &quot;Your character subtracts <b>one</b> from all Difficulty&quot; &quot;reduce any Complication to making a shot due to environmental factors by 1<br /> Change one to 1 to remain consistent with styling of the section.<br /> <br /> p.65 Advanced Combat Maneuvers<br /> Armor Expert<br /> &quot;Characters with this Edge halve the penalty of the Tiring/Bulky tag of any armor.&quot;<br /> Tiring and Bulky tags are not listed in the book","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24507-baladain","name":"Baladain","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-08T15:12:55-08:00","id":1273504,"title":"","content":"p. 169 The &quot;Death Defiance&quot; Gift indicates that a character may use the gift to spend 3 Inspiration and escape death. But, p. 153 indicates that this 3 point expenditure would be a normal aplication of Dramatic Editing &quot;Having a character suddenly reappear after death...costs 3 or more Inspiration, depending on how drastic the change is.&quot; So currently the Gift has no apparent effect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6-slagheap","name":"Slagheap","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"188"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-08T19:12:03-08:00","id":1273536,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Slagheap</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1273286-trinity-continuum-core-errata?p=1273504#post1273504\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">p. 169 The &amp;quot;Death Defiance&amp;quot; Gift indicates that a character may use the gift to spend 3 Inspiration and escape death. But, p. 153 indicates that this 3 point expenditure would be a normal aplication of Dramatic Editing &amp;quot;Having a character suddenly reappear after death...costs 3 or more Inspiration, depending on how drastic the change is.&amp;quot; So currently the Gift has no apparent effect.</div> </div> </div> </div>If the intention is for the latter to apply to NPCs only, that needs to be made more clear.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-08T20:50:52-08:00","id":1273546,"title":"","content":"pg.51 - Walking Wounded &quot;spending 1 Momentum for Bruised or Injured complications&quot; - Complications not capitalized.<br /> pg.64 - PRECISE MARTIAL ARTS &quot;adding + 1 to her Dodge&quot; - Space between \u201c+\u201d and modifier<br /> pg.83 - INFORMATION AS ENHANCEMENT &quot;she might gain a + 3 Enhancement&quot; - Space between \u201c+\u201d and modifier<br /> pg.95 - REFORGING \u2013 last paragraph &quot;Each Flaw costs successes equal to (Flaw dots + item Rank) to fully buy off, or (item Rank + Flaw dots difference)&quot; Successes needed are listed as both \u201cFlaw dots + item Rank\u201d and \u201citem Rank + Flaw dots\u201d<br /> pg.123 - First Paragraph &quot;an additional + 2 Difficulty&quot; Space between \u201c+\u201d and modifier<br /> <br /> \u201cResistance\u201d attribute is referenced multiple times in the text but not defined. It seems like this is referring to the Approach that is defined as \u201cResilience\u201d in the Attribute and Approaches section.<br /> <br /> Complication and Enhancement adjustments in the text are alternatively referred to using the following terms;<br /> \u201clevel # Complication\u201d<br /> \u201c(number spelled out)-point Complication\u201d<br /> \u201c+# Complication\u201d<br /> \u201c# Complication\u201d<br /> This should probably be standardized across the text.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23807,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23807-greenozzy","user":"Greenozzy","date":".  adjusted formatting to increase clarity 12-09-2018, 12:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23807-greenozzy","name":"Greenozzy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23807_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-08T21:50:54-08:00","id":1273551,"title":"","content":"pg.110 \u2013 Damage Examples \u2013 Falling - the Threat Type is listed under the Tags column<br /> pg.121 \u2013 Explosive (Planted) \u201cThe explosive tag means\u201d \u2013 Explosive should be capitalized<br /> pg.123 \u2013 Example Weapons \u2013 Knife \u2013 \u201cThrowing\u201d Tag should be \u201cThrown\u201d<br /> pg.124 \u2013 Composite Armor \u201cThe Composite armor tag\u201d \u2013 Armor should be capitalized<br /> <br /> <br /> The following are all references to Tags that are not defined anywhere in the text;<br /> pg.63 - Deadly Strike - &quot;Slow&quot;<br /> pg.65 - Armor Expert - &quot;Tiring/Bulky&quot;<br /> pg.109 - Damage Examples \u2013 Knock Out Gas - &quot;Cumulative&quot;<br /> pg.117 - 3rd Paragraph - &quot;Shockwave&quot;<br /> pg.118 - 1st Paragraph - &quot;Shockwave&quot;<br /> pg.123 - Variable Ammo - &quot;Electrical&quot;<br /> pg.126 - Armor - &quot;Complete&quot;<br /> pg.213 - Sawed Off - &quot;Unconcealable&quot;<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23807-greenozzy","name":"Greenozzy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23807_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-08T23:43:25-08:00","id":1273557,"title":"","content":"Pg. 39, &quot;Players also use Experience to increase or decrease their degree of Affinity.&quot; This is the only instance of &quot;Affinity&quot; in the text, and is undefined.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3453-nephandi","name":"Nephandi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3453_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-09T10:58:44-08:00","id":1273602,"title":"","content":"p. 15: Chapter One is still listed as &quot;Apocrypha&quot; rather than &quot;Incidentals.&quot;<br /> <br /> p. 30/31: Bianca's faked death on p. 31 predates the whistleblowing action which caused her to be recruited on p. 30. Re-kajigger so it makes better sense.<br /> <br /> p. 139: re: earlier discussion<br /> <br /> p. 212-213: Headers and highlights are in red. Should probably be blue to match with the rest of the book.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1273286-trinity-continuum-core-errata?p=1273536#post1273536\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If the intention is for the latter to apply to NPCs only, that needs to be made more clear.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Please take discussion to another thread.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-09T12:36:57-08:00","id":1273615,"title":"","content":"p.37<br /> <br /> 3 dots in a Skill allow to gain a Skill Trick and an additional Trick for each point above 3 (4+). Each point above 3 (4+) grants a Specialty.<br /> But the example states that the Character gets a Specialty with a 3 dots Skill. Shouldn'it be 4?<br /> <br /> It is also stated the a Character begins with 1 Skill Trick: is it a limit for each 3 dots Skill at the beginning?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2524-sethmes","name":"Sethmes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-09T14:04:39-08:00","id":1273627,"title":"","content":"p.66 - Indomitable<br /> &quot;Your character <b>gain</b> 5 Enhancement&quot; should be <b>gains</b><br /> <br /> p.67 - Respected Authority<br /> This has a prerequisite of Fame 3 but also states &quot;Respected authority provides your character with three dots of Fame&quot; Is this intentional? It would give characters 6 fame, and the fame edge only goes up to 3.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24507-baladain","name":"Baladain","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-09T16:45:07-08:00","id":1273637,"title":"","content":"p.40 - Paths<br /> Is it obvious that the Paths begin at level 1 and that each Path grants 1 contact, 1 group and 1 type of access?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2524-sethmes","name":"Sethmes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-09T23:50:40-08:00","id":1273675,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yue Ryong</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1273286-trinity-continuum-core-errata?p=1273492#post1273492\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bookmarking Issue: Major Allegiances are placed beneath Example CharGen, rather than their own category.</div> </div> </div> </div>Furthermore (and this is probably directly related to Yue Ryong's comment), there's no header for Major Allegiances in the text to introduce the factions, so it seems like 9's entry comes out of nowhere. This is a formatting/layout issue I felt compelled to comment on since I found it so visually jarring.<br /> <br /> Also, Page 164, Arcangel Major Allegiance entry, third paragraph under the &quot;History&quot; heading: The first sentence reads as &quot;He tasked the Luther to create&quot; when it should read &quot;He tasked Luther to create&quot;.<br /> <br /> Also, the separate Character Sheet PDF does not match the layout in the character sheet at the back of the Aeon Continuum corebook. In fact, Gear, Weapons, Armor and Biotech are ALL missing from the separate Character Sheet PDF. The Health Bar is missing from the character sheet at the back of the Aeon Continuum corebook.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/835/7xu8.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/folderview?id=0By9UuUWWH6CiMVlhWHMwNWcyaG8&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Complete Garou Gifts List, Fera Gifts List, Garou Totems List and other assorted OPP/White Wolf goodies</a>","edited":{"userid":2710,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2710-su-tehp","user":"Su-tehp","date":". 12-10-2018, 03:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2710-su-tehp","name":"Su-tehp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2710_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-10T07:57:33-08:00","id":1273719,"title":"","content":"p.39 - Character Advancement<br /> The chart states that 18 Experience are required to improve a Path by 1 dot.<br /> <br /> and<br /> <br /> p.41 - Advancement with paths<br /> Each dot in a Path costs five points of Experience and provides three dots for distribution among the related Skills and two dots for distribution among the related Edges.<br /> <br /> So. 18 or 5 or am I totally mistaken?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2524-sethmes","name":"Sethmes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-10T09:57:49-08:00","id":1273744,"title":"","content":"Pgs 122-123: There seems to be some conflict with how the Ranged tag works and the example weapons. A pistol is tagged as Ranged:Close which doesn't make sense with how the tag is written. The assault rifle lists it as ranged from close to medium with no optimum band as mentioned in the tag. Also the Aeon weapons seem to operate differently from what the Ranged tag description implies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/565-therian","name":"Therian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar565_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-10T10:19:22-08:00","id":1273748,"title":"","content":"Pg. 37. It says, &quot;...but each player also gets<b> six</b> additional dots to distribute among Skills.&quot; Then, in the example box below that, it says, &quot;Weston now has <b>seven</b> final dots to spend on Adrianne from any Skills.&quot;<br /> <br /> Weston then goes on to spend six dots.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8719,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","user":"Florin","date":". 12-10-2018, 02:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-10T12:05:59-08:00","id":1273764,"title":"","content":"p. 38, Health:<br /> &quot;Every character has an Injury Condition tracker.<br /> Every character has three levels of Injury at character creation, Maimed, Injured, and Bruised. At Stamina 3, the character gains an additional Injured Condition and at Stamina 5 the character gains an additional Bruised Condition.&quot;<br /> <br /> Shouldn't it be an additional Injured/bruised level instead of condition? The term condition here implies that you HAVE the condition, meaning you are hurt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3122-shuragil","name":"shuragil","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-10T12:19:09-08:00","id":1273767,"title":"","content":"p. 38, Defense:<br /> &quot;Characters can attempt to make a defensive action when being attacked by rolling the highest of her Resistance Attributes [...]&quot;<br /> Later at the same page, in the blue box below: &quot;Her Defense is 1 and when Weston rolls a defensive action he rolls three dice for her lowest Resistance Attribute [...]&quot;<br /> <br /> So, is it the highest or lowest Resistance attribute to roll here?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3122-shuragil","name":"shuragil","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-10T18:43:52-08:00","id":1273819,"title":"","content":"p.71 Two halves to every challenge.<br /> &quot;her dice pool and the target number she wants each <b>dice</b>&quot; should be each <b>die</b><br /> <br /> p.72 Complications<br /> \u201cA Complication is separate from the overall Difficulty of the task and <b>do</b> not affect\u201d should be &quot;<b>does </b>not affect&quot;<br /> <br /> p.77 Completing Milestones<br /> &quot;Success and failure each use up one <b>attempts</b>&quot; should be one <b>attempt</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24507,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24507-baladain","user":"Baladain","date":". 12-12-2018, 11:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24507-baladain","name":"Baladain","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-11T03:57:10-08:00","id":1273864,"title":"","content":"p.63 - Forceful Martial Arts<br /> <br /> Your character knows how to fight in a brutal and direct manner using either brawling or a single type of hand to hand weapon, like chain weapons, <b><i>cubs</i></b>, fists and feet, or swords. You can purchase this Edge multiple times, but each purchase only applies to a single type of weapon.<br /> <br /> &quot;clubs&quot;, no?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2524-sethmes","name":"Sethmes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-11T04:33:02-08:00","id":1273868,"title":"","content":"p.195 - Speak Softly<br /> <br /> &quot;Something about putting both hands on a weapon brings out a strength in her that she never knew before. She isn\u2019t just <i><b>indimating </b></i>when carrying a large weapon, she\u2019s downright deadly.&quot;<br /> <br /> Intimidating?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2524-sethmes","name":"Sethmes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-11T06:16:31-08:00","id":1273876,"title":"","content":"Page 103<br /> <br /> In Scion Dive to Cover was changed to specify it could only be used against ranged attacks. Should this be the case with Trinity?<br /> <br /> Roll Away as written is potentially problematic if it allows you to avoid a melee attack entirely by shifting outside of the attack range. I made a post about this with Scion that is still being discussed.<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1235662-the-roll-away-defensive-stunt-is-problimatic-for-the-future-of-scion-2nd\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1235662-the-roll-away-defensive-stunt-is-problimatic-for-the-future-of-scion-2nd\"> The Roll Away Defensive Stunt Is Problimatic For the Future of Scion 2nd - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1235662-the-roll-away-defensive-stunt-is-problimatic-for-the-future-of-scion-2nd\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1235662-the-roll-away-defensive-stunt-is-problimatic-for-the-future-of-scion-2nd </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Bold Statement, But I will break down why this option is damaging to the future of the game. I mentioned this to Neall and he suggested I made a post about it. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9236-yig1015w","name":"Yig1015w","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"182"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-11T06:29:23-08:00","id":1273877,"title":"","content":"p.155 - Life-threatening incident.<br /> <br /> The header is not formatted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2524-sethmes","name":"Sethmes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-11T06:40:57-08:00","id":1273879,"title":"","content":"Character Sheet<br /> <br /> Larceny has become &quot;Larcency&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2524-sethmes","name":"Sethmes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-12T12:44:10-08:00","id":1274096,"title":"","content":"p.79-80 Combat Attributes: &quot;The Attribute required for dice pools to affect targets with appropriate weapons&quot;, chart on p.79 specifies Might as the appropriate combat attribute.<br /> However, the examples given for Close Combat: (p.47) give examples for using Might, Stamina, Dexterity and Cunning that are all applicable in the close range band.<br /> Since these two items directly contradict, suggest removing the Combat attribute column from the chart on p.79, and from the description on p.80<br /> <br /> p.80 Range &quot;Each range possesses the following characteristics.&quot; Justification inconsistent with other entries<br /> p.83 Analysis, Information: &quot;Interpetation, QA, Player Creation&quot; Justification inconsistent with other entries<br /> p.84 Hacking &quot;an appropriate specialty (cryptography or Software) is always required&quot; Does not appear to be consistent with the way specialties are used in this rulebook","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24507-baladain","name":"Baladain","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-13T04:40:40-08:00","id":1274172,"title":"","content":"p. 73 - Momentum: second paragraph mentions the Black Pool several times","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24911-dulthar","name":"Dulthar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-13T07:34:27-08:00","id":1274199,"title":"","content":"Missing bookmark for &quot;Difficulty&quot; in the PDF (p.72)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2524-sethmes","name":"Sethmes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-13T12:23:57-08:00","id":1274233,"title":"","content":"On p. 38 of the core rules book you state in the text that you roll the highest Resistence Attribute to purchase defensive stunts while the blue box states the opposite.<br /> <br /> Also, on p. 103 in hte description of Ambushes, there is an &quot;agility&quot; skill mentioned. I don't find it anywhere else, and I think that should be Larceny.<br /> <br /> Also, and I know the book is kinda done, but could you smuggle a reference into the &quot;Paths&quot; section of character creation, that states that the society paths are in the back of the book with the allegiances. It took me a few minutes to figure that one out.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24928-quantum-bob","name":"Quantum Bob","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-13T14:50:26-08:00","id":1274254,"title":"","content":"p. 93 Milestones and time<br /> &quot;The descriptions <b>below</b> are a guideline...&quot; The chart is above this text, not below.<br /> <br /> p.95 Super-Science Specialties<br /> Are these specialties for the Science or Engineering skills? Should they be treated as edges? Are they just &quot;styles&quot; selected for the character?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24507-baladain","name":"Baladain","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-13T17:34:53-08:00","id":1274281,"title":"","content":"p.60 Fast Draw &quot;Drawing or holstering that weapon is considered a reflexive action.&quot;<br /> p.99 &quot;Reflexive actions in combat represent activities that take little to no time to perform. Actions such as looking around, <b>retrieving objects from a holster</b>...are all considered reflexive actions&quot;<br /> Based on the examples of reflexive actions on p.99, the <b>Fast Draw</b> edge provides no actual benefit.<br /> <br /> p.99 &quot;When it is a character\u2019s turn to act, they can take any number of different actions (equal to their Cunning). Actions fall into three broad categories: reflexive,ordinary, and mixed.&quot;<br /> Does this mean that a character with cunning three can draw a weapon (reflexive action) shoot two targets while lobbing a grenade (mixed action, limited to 3 per this phrase on p.101 &quot;The limit<br /> to the number of mixed actions a player can take as part of a single action roll is equal to his Cunning.&quot;) and then dive behind cover (defensive action)?<br /> Thereby totaling six actions? Or does the limit on &quot;different actions&quot; on p.99 include multiple actions taken as part of a mixed action?<br /> <br /> p.100 Initiative<br /> &quot;That character gets <b>the</b> Focus, acts, and chooses who from their team will get Focus next.&quot; <b>the</b> should be removed.<br /> <br /> p.101 Attacking<br /> &quot;Attack actions have a Difficulty of 1, which may be modified by the target\u2019s Dodge Stunt.&quot;<br /> Shouldn't this state that Attack actions have a difficulty equal to the target's Defense rating? Otherwise this seems to imply you need 1 base success + 1 attack action success + 1 target defense success. Then modified by stunts, and so forth. on p.102 - close combat strike it states &quot;Hit: Overcome the opponent's Defense&quot; which is much more clear.<br /> <br /> p.101 Attacking - Example:<br /> &quot;After he declares the attacks, his opponents roll for <b>defending</b>&quot; Should be roll for defense.<br /> <br /> p.102 Close combat strike - Inflict damage<br /> Difficulty is listed as &quot;Opponent's Armor&quot; instead of &quot;1 success + opponent's Armor&quot; as is listed for Shoot and Thrown Attack<br /> <br /> p.103 Defense &quot;Penalties to Defense from sources such as Injury Conditions can never bring the character\u2019s Defense below 1.&quot;<br /> p.105 Bruised &quot;Bruised Ribs, -1 Defense&quot;<br /> p.105 Injured &quot;Cracked Ribs, -2 Defense&quot;<br /> Seems completely contradictory, that you can have these penalties and still not have your Defense reduced to 0. Also, wouldn't an unconscious/unaware/paralyzed person have a Defense of 0?<br /> <br /> p. 104 Condition Levels<br /> &quot;Any time the character takes damage, he must fill in an Injury Condition box. His player must choose to take a Bruised, Injured, or Maimed Condition, if available. If none are available, he is Taken Out.&quot;<br /> p.105 Taken Out<br /> &quot;When a character is all out of Condition boxes, he is Taken Out.&quot;<br /> The statement on 104 implies that the character is taken out when they are Maimed and take one more Injury Condition.<br /> The statement on 105 imples that the character is taken out when they become Maimed.<br /> <br /> p.105 Taken Out<br /> &quot;A player can choose to fill in the Taken Out box at any time, rather than take potentially long-lasting Injury Complications.&quot;<br /> Neither the Core nor Aeon sheets provided with these pdfs have a &quot;Taken Out Box&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> p. 109 Damage Examples<br /> Falling damage is not correctly formatted to table.<br /> <br /> p.111-112 Sample Combat<br /> &quot;Ariadne has a Close Combat of 4 and a Might of 3, so her total dice pool for this action is 7.&quot;<br /> &quot;Colton\u2019s player rolls his Aim (5) + Cunning (4)&quot;<br /> please standardize format.<br /> <br /> Sample Combat mentions Arena Rating several times, but this does not appear anywhere else in the book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24507-baladain","name":"Baladain","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-13T17:37:13-08:00","id":1274282,"title":"","content":"Issues with Successes V. Difficulty<br /> <br /> p.101 Combat Roll example<br /> &quot;breaking the restraints is a Difficulty 1 (Athletics + Might) check and that kicking the Bomb is a Difficulty 0 (Close Combat + Might) check. Disarming is fairly difficult, but the thug is not terribly competent so disarming him is only Difficulty 1 (Close Combat + Might) action. If Jason wants to accomplish everything he\u2019s set out to do this turn he will need five successes.<br /> <br /> In this combat roll example, completing a difficulty 1 task, (disarm thug, break bonds) required 2 successes each<br /> <br /> p.107 Damage Rating<br /> &quot;All sources of indirect damage have a Difficulty of 1. On a successful roll, each remaining success subtracts one from the damage rating.&quot;<br /> &quot;For example, if a character drank a cocktail someone laced with cyanide (damage rating 5), she would need to make a Stamina + Resolve roll. If she rolled four successes, she succeeded, because she exceeded the Difficulty and thus her three remaining successes would subtract from the Damage Rating, reducing it from 5 to 2.&quot;<br /> These examples treat difficulty differently.<br /> <br /> In this Damage Rating section, completing a difficulty 1 task (resisting the poison, indirect damage, difficulty 1) only required 1 success (4 successes rolled, 3 success left, damage reduced from 5 to 2)<br /> <br /> <br /> p.111 Sample Combat<br /> &quot;bringing her total successes to three. She spends the first success against the Difficulty (Defense of 1, so Difficulty 1) to hit her opponent. She then has two remaining successes to spend on Stunts. Fin isn\u2019t wearing any armor, so she purchases the \u201cInflict Damage\u201d Stunt for one success. With her one remaining success, Ariadne\u2019s player purchases the Feint Stunt, granting her an Enhancement bonus of 1 on her next attack against<br /> Fin.&quot;<br /> <br /> In this Sample Combat section, completing a difficulty 1 task (attacking fin) only required 1 success. 2 rolled, 1 enhancement, 3 total. spend 1 for difficulty (defense rating) 1 for inflict damage and 1 for feint<br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;He nets an additional two successes as an Enhancement bonus for his revolver, bringing his total to five. their Defense is 1, Colton\u2019s player spends one success to hit the mob; he then spends one success to inflict the Taken Out condition on the first henchman since he is not wearing any armor. Colton repeats this for the next two henchmen. He has one remaining success that he decides not to use.<br /> <br /> in this Sample Combat section, completing a difficulty 1 task (attacking the mob) also only required 1 success. 5 total, 1 spent to hit the mob 3 spent to inflict damage on each henchman, 1 remaining.<br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;Colton...purchases the Dodge Stunt, bringing his Defense to 2. The Storyguide spends two successes to hit&quot;<br /> <br /> difficulty 2 task, only 2 successes used.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24507-baladain","name":"Baladain","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-13T23:35:05-08:00","id":1274314,"title":"","content":"In the character creation section, the character creation summary page is missing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-14T04:50:18-08:00","id":1274342,"title":"","content":"P. 83 In the attitude example: \u201cIf the auction is full, he\u2019ll just have to get someone booted from the party so the he can fill the vacancy.\u201c<br /> <br /> Should this read \u201c...so that he can fill the vacancy.\u201d","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24911-dulthar","name":"Dulthar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-14T05:57:14-08:00","id":1274354,"title":"","content":"p.74<br /> I have the feeling that the header levels are kind of messed up in the Conditions and fields section. Fields, time, actions, round...<br /> <br /> Edit : Complex actions header should be at the same level as Round-by-round actions, Milestones a sub-level. I don't know what to do with Types of complex actions and its sub-headers, formatted with a blue background. The whole thing is barely understandable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2524,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2524-sethmes","user":"Sethmes","date":". 12-19-2018, 10:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2524-sethmes","name":"Sethmes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-15T00:50:24-08:00","id":1274513,"title":"","content":"Not sure if this is errata or simply a normal convention, but everyone in the Credits (p. 2) is listed alphabetically except the artists, who don\u2019t appear to be in any order.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-15T01:55:31-08:00","id":1274519,"title":"","content":"This one\u2019s incredibly pedantic, but to avoid *any* reader confusion:<br /> <br /> P.15, 2nd dot point - &quot;All dice showing the target number are successes&quot; - should read &quot;All dice showing the target number or higher are successes&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-15T02:06:30-08:00","id":1274521,"title":"","content":"Lexicon, p.17. Psiads don\u2019t require the rumoured in &quot;rumoured psions who gained their powers naturally&quot;, readers know they exist by their upcoming rules in the AEon AExpansion. The final sentence &quot;Their existence is a popular, but un-proven, urban legend&quot;, provides the setting detail.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-15T02:15:14-08:00","id":1274523,"title":"","content":"P.40 - unless the Continuum is operating off a different timeline, 4 April 2018 was a Wednesday, not a Saturday. (The in-universe artifacts on p. 18 correctly lists 7 March 2018 as a Wednesday, suggesting the April date is an error.)<br /> <br /> Same on p. 31, with 3 February 2018 not being a Monday, and 6 February not being a Thursday.<br /> <br /> (P. 32 got it right.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":156,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","user":"Bunyip","date":". 12-15-2018, 05:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-15T02:30:30-08:00","id":1274524,"title":"","content":"P.37, final dot point, column 1 - specifies all Paths have a &quot;Path Condition that triggers when you invoke the Path too often&quot;, but neither the example Path Weston builds immediately after this nor any Path in Core or AEon include a Path Condition. Is this a remnant of an earlier system design?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-15T02:34:51-08:00","id":1274525,"title":"","content":"P.39 - Experience awards for characters have the column title &quot;Experience Cost&quot;, implying a character has to pay experience to achieve these roleplaying events.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-15T02:50:02-08:00","id":1274528,"title":"","content":"Arc - players can spend Experience at the end of an Arc (p. 39), and long-term aspirations are something that take an Arc to achieve (p. 35), but an \u2018Arc\u2019 doesn\u2019t appear to be defined as a Storypath time period. Rank 4 Super-Science (p. 93) also requires \u2018one story arc\u2019 for a milestone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-15T02:59:59-08:00","id":1274530,"title":"","content":"AEon refers to psions as Tier 2 and Proxies as Tier 3 but the Tier chart on p. 71 has no numerical values for tiers. (The numbers match up to the \u2018Relative Scale\u2019 table on p. 74 though.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":156,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","user":"Bunyip","date":". 12-15-2018, 06:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-15T13:59:44-08:00","id":1274620,"title":"","content":"Talents, p. 150 says &quot;Once per scene, a player may add one of her Facet's rating as an Enhancement to an action that furthers a goal, if she is acting in a way in line with that Facet's concept of Intention, Skill or Luck&quot;, then p.151, the character can spend one Inspiration to activate Destructive Action, Intuitive Action, or Reflective Action to essentially do the same thing. <br /> <br /> Is it intentional that the first use is free, then subsequent require Inspiration spend, or loose wording between the two close sections?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-15T14:01:36-08:00","id":1274621,"title":"","content":"p. 115 Station: Contact<br /> &quot;...deciphering coded or garbled messages, <b>relying</b> crucial orders or messages&quot; should be <b>relaying</b><br /> <br /> p.116 2,500 tons of awesome<br /> &quot;<b>No matter well</b> a player rolls,&quot; should be No matter <b>how</b> well<br /> <br /> &quot;Likewise, vehicles make excellent use of <b>Power</b> rules&quot;<br /> &quot;Conversely, <b>Power</b> can be also employed&quot;<br /> &quot;an infantryman can carry a missile launcher specifically designed to negate a tank\u2019s <b>Power</b> advantage&quot;<br /> &quot;a character faced with an armored vehicle with prohibitive <b>Power</b>&quot;<br /> should these instances of <b>Power</b> be <b>Scale</b>?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24507-baladain","name":"Baladain","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-15T14:13:57-08:00","id":1274622,"title":"","content":"Breath Control p.60 - If a character can hold her breath Stamina x 8 (motionless) or Stamina x 4 (active) minutes, why does she need to check for suffocation damage every 8 or 4 minutes. Does her Stamina have an effect or not? <br /> <br /> Also, Core doesn\u2019t appear to include suffocation damage rules. AEon includes drowning, but not Core.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-15T14:20:32-08:00","id":1274623,"title":"","content":"P.63 - The Free Running dot titles aren\u2019t bolded like other Style Edges.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-15T22:02:01-08:00","id":1274667,"title":"","content":"(Copied to AEon thread as well.)<br /> What is \u2018Health\u2019 on the character sheet? Both sheets already include Injury Conditions. Appears to be a holdover from WoD/CoD character sheets.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-16T12:29:53-08:00","id":1274752,"title":"","content":"Core appears to be lacking key rules for Momentum, such as how many you start with (even if none), whether they carry over between sessions, and whether you have to add dice to a pool before or after seeing a roll\u2019s results. (P. 72 implies that you can spend afterwards, but is that spending one Momentum to gain one die and rolling that, seeing if it helps and then spending another, ad so on?)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-16T12:53:52-08:00","id":1274756,"title":"","content":"p28, red script under the ANGEL CULT SURRENDERS article, 3rd sentence, reads as,<b> &quot;</b>UFO and meteor reports from s<br /> even independent sources across county overnight.&quot; Is probably intended to read as, &quot;... from seven independent sources...&quot; (the word &quot;seven&quot; has an [Enter] between the &quot;s&quot; and &quot;even&quot;.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23804,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23804-uri-meca","user":"Uri Meca","date":".  Edit: Close parenthesis 12-16-2018, 04:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23804-uri-meca","name":"Uri Meca","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-16T15:54:23-08:00","id":1274796,"title":"","content":"p.123 Reach<br /> &quot;Reach weapons gain +1 Enhancement when using Complicate <b>Action</b>.&quot; Action should be Stunt<br /> <br /> p.123 Thrown<br /> &quot;Thrown weapons can be used in both close and short range with no penalty.&quot; seems this should be short range only, as throwing something at someone close enough to grab you is impractical<br /> <br /> p.123 Variable Ammo<br /> The ammunition tags listed are not present in this book.<br /> <br /> p.123 example weapons<br /> Assault Rifle has &quot;Quality&quot; should be &quot;Quality 2&quot;<br /> Katana has &quot;quality&quot; and &quot;quality 2&quot; listed. &quot;quality&quot; should be removed<br /> Pistol has &quot;ranged: close&quot; should be &quot;ranged: short&quot;<br /> Stun Gun has enhancement 1, should be 2 as per <b>charge </b>tag<br /> <br /> p.124 Worn<br /> &quot;some <b>way.Worn</b> weapons&quot; Space needed after way.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24507-baladain","name":"Baladain","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-16T16:32:55-08:00","id":1274801,"title":"","content":"p. 126 Armor<br /> &quot;All vehicle armor possesses the Complete tag&quot; Complete tag is not present in this book.<br /> <br /> p. 126 Maneuverable is missing its formatting box<br /> <br /> p. 126 Massive<br /> &quot;Each additional Size rank also adds an additional Condition box.&quot; Unable to locate starting number of condition boxes for vehicles<br /> <br /> p. 126 Military<br /> &quot;People <b>with</b> a military Path or related Specialty suffer a level 3 Complication&quot; Should be people <b>with-out</b><br /> <br /> p. 127 Example Vehicles table<br /> Sports car has &quot;Wheeled 0&quot; should be changed to &quot;Wheeled&quot; for consistency<br /> ATV has too many tags for it's cost.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24507-baladain","name":"Baladain","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-16T21:09:47-08:00","id":1274829,"title":"","content":"The combat example does not use the same mechanics as are described for Antagonists. It talks about arenas, and says that mooks have a flat defense of 1/4 an arena and don't roll defense actions. The rules for minor characters on p138 (which I assume aren't the &quot;minor threats&quot; on page 137) say that they use their desperation pool for defense but don't roll defense actions. What do they do with their desperation pool then?<br /> <br /> Why does the character sheet give everyone 5 conditions when they only start with 3?<br /> <br /> Do health boxes for antagonists behave like injury conditions (1 injury stunt = 1 box, 1 injury stunt per attack) or are the rules different? Since health boxes don't seem to apply negative effects to antagonists like injury conditions do to PCs that seems to be a problem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24935-werlynn","name":"werlynn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"192"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-16T23:32:27-08:00","id":1274842,"title":"","content":"P.38 - you gain an extra Injured at Stamina 3 and an extra Bruised at Stamina 5. The character sheet is including enough stat boxes for any starting character. Simply cross off any a character doesn\u2019t have.<br /> <br /> Edit: Apologies - realised this was the errata thread, not the discussion thread.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-17T12:56:24-08:00","id":1274940,"title":"","content":"p. 137 Natural Weapons<br /> &quot;It may have elongated teeth, <b>sharped</b> claws&quot; should be either sharp or sharpened.<br /> <br /> p. 123 Weighted - This should be limited to Melee weapons. ranged weapon projectiles lack the mass required to push people around, and if they do have that much mass, there's nothing left of the target to push anywhere.<br /> <br /> p.64-65 Sniper - Trick shot - this should not be able to grant the weighted tag. See above.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24507-baladain","name":"Baladain","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-17T16:31:56-08:00","id":1274983,"title":"","content":"The following pages reference episodes as a unit of time. I believe this is meant to be session.<br /> <br /> p. 88 Love - Action<br /> p. 134 Challenging the players and the characters<br /> p. 152 Regaining inspiration","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24507-baladain","name":"Baladain","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-17T19:41:35-08:00","id":1275006,"title":"","content":"Character sheets (Psion &amp; Talent) lack space to record specialties.<br /> <br /> Edit: While we're at it, some manner of formal clarification as to what happens to Specialties &amp; Skill Tricks if you Tweak a Skill down below 3 dots would be nice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>---------------------------------------------<br /> Supporter of Spirits getting full playable splat design come Exalted 3E.<br /> Refugee from the 3rd Great Edition Wars of D&amp;D. <br /> oWoD Latecomer, Exalted Optimist, Scion ST, Trinity Curious","edited":{"userid":955,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/955-yue-ryong","user":"Yue Ryong","date":". 12-17-2018, 11:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/955-yue-ryong","name":"Yue Ryong","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar955_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"147"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-17T23:25:34-08:00","id":1275034,"title":"","content":"Page 109 no terminal volocity damage cap for falling damage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6424,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6424-fuzzykuma","user":"Fuzzykuma","date":". 12-18-2018, 05:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6424-fuzzykuma","name":"Fuzzykuma","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6424_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"178"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-20T08:01:20-08:00","id":1275515,"title":"","content":"Hi, not sure if this is errata or a misunderstanding of the text but:<br /> <br /> How does Armor work with antagonists? As antagonists have soft Armour and dodge rolled into one stat as &quot;Defence&quot; does this need to be beaten for every inflict damage stunt? Other Tags that are thrown into question<br /> How is Piercing adjudicated if armour is not clearly defined, its it always a -1 to defence? <br /> When/ How can non penetrating apply? <br /> How can Gas bypass armor when it is rolled into 1 stat. <br /> I haven't read Aeon but this may apply there? I get the impression from some of the anomaly powers that Soft Armour should not be rolled into defence but instead applied on top of the defence trait as described in pg 136<br /> <br /> Most of the combat rules work fine when applied against another full player sheet, but the stripped down Antagonist rules these confusions happen. If I am misreading or misunderstanding the rules please PM me as this also has confused me with Scion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Find my Homebrew so far here: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/18X_mkFwDcM0sSN9R2GoQ72Q5FqW1deFgEM3HIGneABQ/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...it?usp=sharing</a><br /> So far its Demon Merits, Vampire 1e to 2e ports and a Knowledge collection mechanic for the Ordo Dracul!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24597-lordofiron","name":"LordofIron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24597_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-20T12:10:48-08:00","id":1275591,"title":"","content":"p. 200 After-School Special: This gift reads as though the character can sway an entire group of minor characters, regardless of number. Is this accurate? Clarification may be needed.<br /> <br /> p. 204 Fortean Experience: &quot;If she has the correct Science Specialty, you may spend an inspiration to know the effects of the alteration&quot; Does not appear consistent with the way Specialties are defined on p. 45","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24507-baladain","name":"Baladain","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-20T13:54:40-08:00","id":1275621,"title":"","content":"Character Sheets have indicators for Skill Tricks to have dot ratings, but nowhere in the system do Skill Tricks have ratings.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>---------------------------------------------<br /> Supporter of Spirits getting full playable splat design come Exalted 3E.<br /> Refugee from the 3rd Great Edition Wars of D&amp;D. <br /> oWoD Latecomer, Exalted Optimist, Scion ST, Trinity Curious","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/955-yue-ryong","name":"Yue Ryong","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar955_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"147"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-21T02:12:09-08:00","id":1275751,"title":"","content":"Mixed Actions:<br /> PG 70 - No limit on number of actions that can be done at once is mentioned<br /> PG 101 - &quot;<span style=\"font-size:10px\">The limit to the number of mixed actions a player can take as part of a single action roll is equal to his Cunning.&quot;<br /> Is this a discrepancy or does the Cunning limit only apply in combat.<br /> <br /> Also Failing Mixed Actions: Do players get 1 momentum for each action failed, or one for the whole die pool. Otherwise you can attempt 6 actions, fail 5 and generate a lot of momentum.<br /> <br /> Also PG 73 - Reference to the Black Pool. Does momentum have an upper limit in the pool in Trinity? (Also could you ask the scion guys that as their book doesn't say either!)</span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Find my Homebrew so far here: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/18X_mkFwDcM0sSN9R2GoQ72Q5FqW1deFgEM3HIGneABQ/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...it?usp=sharing</a><br /> So far its Demon Merits, Vampire 1e to 2e ports and a Knowledge collection mechanic for the Ordo Dracul!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24597-lordofiron","name":"LordofIron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24597_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-21T18:11:50-08:00","id":1275965,"title":"","content":"p73 - Scale needs more clarification and examples as it's a big concept discussed <br /> very briefly and quickly. Is a Psion automatically better at everything than a normal human, or just matters that are direct arenas of competition (e.g. playing chess)? An example of narrative scale, even a basic, one would be good.<br /> <br /> p113 - There are no vehicle combat rules or rules about driving and piloting. Were the rules from Scion supposed to get pasted in here?<br /> <br /> Consider an appendix of pre-made equipment and gadgets using the super science system - <br /> Shadowrun Anarchy had a 'build your own power' system and but added an appendix of <br /> prebuilt powers while in layout (at the end where it wouldn't muck up the existing layout) and we've used it heavily.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23864-khelbiros","name":"Khelbiros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23864_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-23T10:33:35-08:00","id":1276279,"title":"","content":"p. 123, Example Weapons, range for Assault Rifle should propably be short - medium, range for Pistol should propably be short.<br /> <br /> Consider giving Assault Rifles the Two Handed tag, to represent the extra Oomph of these Weapons.<br /> <br /> p. 112, Example Combat could use a reference for minor characters and mobs. The Physical Arena Rating from the same pages alse seems to be gone, and seemingly was replaced by Mob rules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24928,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24928-quantum-bob","user":"Quantum Bob","date":". 12-23-2018, 01:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24928-quantum-bob","name":"Quantum Bob","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-23T14:23:19-08:00","id":1276319,"title":"","content":"On page 77, it seems odd that the rubric &quot;Complex actions&quot; is considerably smaller and less bold than the rubric &quot;Milestones&quot; that should reasonably be a subheader to the aforementioned.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9849-aristarkos","name":"Aristarkos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9849_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-25T04:52:43-08:00","id":1276600,"title":"","content":"p90-97: Super-Science Items lack a clear indication of their effective Wealth rating for the purposes of calculating how many tags Weapon-, Armour- or Vehicle-type Super-Science equipment may have.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>---------------------------------------------<br /> Supporter of Spirits getting full playable splat design come Exalted 3E.<br /> Refugee from the 3rd Great Edition Wars of D&amp;D. <br /> oWoD Latecomer, Exalted Optimist, Scion ST, Trinity Curious","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/955-yue-ryong","name":"Yue Ryong","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar955_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"147"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-25T21:27:07-08:00","id":1276742,"title":"","content":"p48 Command, Example rolls using Command: &quot;Given an inspiring speech (+Presence)&quot; meant to read as &quot;<b>Giving</b> an inspiring speech (+ Presence)&quot;?<br /> \u200bIf your character is issuing a Command off an inspiring speech another character made, I could see an argument for &quot;Given an inspiring speech (+ <b>speech-giver's</b> Presence).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23804-uri-meca","name":"Uri Meca","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-26T08:49:27-08:00","id":1276804,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trinity: Core, p73</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Narrative Scale describes the multiplier you<br /> should apply to successes, or to the trait itself for resisted<br /> rolls.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wording is ambiguous enough to cause confusion. Recommend adding ', equal to the Scale rating' to the end of the sentence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>---------------------------------------------<br /> Supporter of Spirits getting full playable splat design come Exalted 3E.<br /> Refugee from the 3rd Great Edition Wars of D&amp;D. <br /> oWoD Latecomer, Exalted Optimist, Scion ST, Trinity Curious","edited":{"userid":955,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/955-yue-ryong","user":"Yue Ryong","date":". 12-26-2018, 12:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/955-yue-ryong","name":"Yue Ryong","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar955_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"147"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-26T17:52:09-08:00","id":1276906,"title":"","content":"p45 Skill Tricks says <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> When you reach level 3 in a Skill, you can choose one Skill Trick for that Skill. As your character advances in the Skill, you can choose an additional Skill Trick for each Dot above 3 as well. Characters begin game with one Skill Trick in a Skill rated 3 or higher. </div> </div> </div><ol class=\"decimal\"><li>This seems contradictory in the case of beginning characters. Does a beginning character with Aim 4 gain begin the game with <i>one</i> skill trick as per the last sentence? Or 2 skill points as per the first and second sentences? It is unclear. If the skill tricks are intended to be <i>purchased</i>, that is not evident as the wording suggests they're free.On page 39, it lists 3 Experience as the cost for a skill trick. Is this in order to purchase extra ones? Or is the &quot;one skill trick at level 3 plus one per dot above 3&quot; rule intended as a cap on how many skill tricks it is possible to have at one time?</li> <li>Last sentence, even if correct with respect to skill tricks, should probably read as, &quot;Characters begin <b>the</b> game with one Skill Trick....&quot;</li> </ol>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23804-uri-meca","name":"Uri Meca","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-27T15:35:10-08:00","id":1277101,"title":"","content":"p16 - The heading is 'Books and Comics' but no Comics are listed, just books.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23864-khelbiros","name":"Khelbiros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23864_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-27T23:07:01-08:00","id":1277153,"title":"","content":"Inconsistent Language and mechanics for Paths:<br /> <br /> <b>Terminology</b><br /> <br /> p 36 &quot;In Trinity Continuum each character has three Paths:<b> Origin</b>, <b>Profession</b>, and<b> Society</b>.&quot;<br /> p36 &quot;The Origin Path is a character's background...&quot; &quot;The <b>Role</b> Path is a charter's occupation or area of expertise...&quot; &quot;The Soceity Path is a connection each charater has with a larger organization...&quot;<br /> p 41 discusses Origin Paths; p 43 discusses <b>Role</b> Paths. No discussion of Society Paths (ah sorry, yes there is, under Chapter Six: Talents, p153 Creating Talents, &quot;Talents should choose their <b>Society</b> Path from the <b>Allegiances</b> listed on p. XX.&quot;)<br /> p 154 <b>Society</b> Paths: <b>Allegiances, &quot;</b>Talents call these groups <b>Allegiances</b>, and nearly every Talent belongs to one or another of the groups.&quot;<br /> p 214 Character Sheet: Origin Path, <b>Role </b>Path, <b>Allegiance</b> Path. (Will any Continuum setting refer to their Soceity Path organizations as &quot;Societies&quot;? If not, why not simply call the path Allegiance on p 36?)(Ah, I see, Aeon seems to consistently refer to them as Soceity Paths.)<br /> <br /> <b>Starting Path rating</b><br /> <br /> p. 36, 1st parag con't from p 35, &quot;You gain three dots to distribute among the four Skills for each Path.&quot; and 3rd parag, &quot;Players gain two dots to distribute among the Edges associated with each Path.&quot;<br /> Pp 36-37 does not list a 1-5 rating as one of the elements of a Path<br /> p 40, 2nd paragraph, &quot;A Path also has a rating from 1 to 5. Each additional dot in a Path strengthens the associated connections, Skills, and Edges&quot;;<br /> p 41, Advancement With Paths, 2nd paragraph, &quot;Each dot in a Path costs five points of Experience and provides three dots for distribution among the related Skills and two dots for distribution among the related Edges.&quot;<br /> <br /> It is never stated that Paths start with rating 1 or 1 dot but it seems to be the case given the dots of skills/edges for character creation when compared to what one gets during advancement.<br /> Someone else pointed out inconsistent advancement cost of Paths, 5 points on p41 vs 18 points on the table on p 39.<br /> <br /> <b>Connections</b> P 40<br /> <br /> 1<sup>st</sup> parag: \u201c<b>Each</b> Path has three different connections: group, contact, and access.<b>\u201d</b><br /> 2<sup>nd</sup> parag: \u201cThe player chooses one contact connection.\u201d<br /> 2<sup>nd</sup> column, under \u201cContacts\u201d heading: 1<sup>st</sup> parag: \u201cShe begins play with a single Contact.\u201d Seems to be immediately contradicted by the following paragraph, \u201cShe can spend these dots on either <b>gaining additional Contacts</b>, or making a single Contact better.\u201d<br /> 2<sup>nd</sup> parag: \u201d A character gains a number of points to use to create her Contacts as she has dots in her Path.\u201d<br /> <br /> So, does the character begin play with a single Contact, total? Or one contact per Path? How many dots does one start with in a Path? Can you start with more than one? It\u2019s not explicit. How does one advance Contacts? When the Path advances? Path advancement lists only dots for skills and edges, not contacts. There is no entry for contacts on the advancement table.<br /> <br /> P 40, Also under \u201c<b>Contacts</b>\u201d: \u201cEach Contact begins with one dot and one tag ... Each additional dot placed in a single Contact adds an additional tag. Tags define the types of rolls a Contact can help your character with, and add the Storyguide char\u00adacter\u2019s dot rating as an Enhancement to those rolls.\u201d<br /> <br /> Great idea\u2026 but they don\u2019t appear to define much other than in the one example with the Influential tag. If anything, tags seem to <i>suggest</i> how a contact might be helpful, rather than define it. What is the difference between a Group connection and a Contact connection with the \u201cnumerous\u201d tag?<br /> <br /> p40 <b>Contacts</b> entry elaborates on that type of Connection. If there are supposed to be similar entries and mechanics for the other types of connections (Group and Access), those are missing.<br /> <br /> p41<b> Using Connections</b>:<br /> 2<sup>nd</sup> parag: \u201cInitially, each connection has the same dot rat\u00ading as the overall Path.\u201d<br /> <br /> That is elegant but seems contradicted by what was explained for Contacts since additional dots can instead be used to gain other contacts? Is the intent to allow characters to gain other Groups and Access as well? Are groups and access intended to have tags?<br /> <br /> The examples that follow for Origin Paths and Role Paths inconsistently include examples of group and contact connections and consistently exclude examples of access connections. Later on, with the Allegiances, each one offers sample Contact connections but not sample Group or Access connections. It would be helpful in each Origin Path, Role Path and Allegiance to give examples of each type of connection in a consistent format, e.g. group/contact/access.<br /> <br /> That\u2019s a lot of nit-picking. I must add I do love how the whole Paths thing is shaping up. It seems like wonderfully collaborative exercise between storyguide and player that, once accomplished with the whole group, would result in strong contributions to the world-building. I love that you have a simple mechanic that helps prevent Connection abuse with the suspension and revoking of connections.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23804-uri-meca","name":"Uri Meca","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-29T02:28:27-08:00","id":1277316,"title":"","content":"Moving and maneuvering really need to be clarified and cleaned. This part seems to have been forgotten or not actually implemented in the round sequence.<br /> p. 80 and 81, we talk about clash, near, far ranges while the chart mentions close, short, medium, long, extreme, out of range.<br /> <br /> The way movements can be used is obscure. Do we have one movement per round ? Can we use &quot;2&quot; movements to go further than &quot;near/short&quot; range ?<br /> <br /> Why this difference between Complicated and Difficult terrains? What about this complex action for Difficult terrains? No example. It sounds like a mixed action but remains very sketchy.<br /> Sprinting is also barely understandable. What does mean &quot;moving from near to far or beyond&quot;?<br /> <br /> In my opinion, a part that important in<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2524-sethmes","name":"Sethmes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-30T01:09:39-08:00","id":1277464,"title":"","content":"What are Attribute maximums for most characters? (And for other higher Tier characters?) p. 37 says \u201cAttributes are rated 1-6, though only Talents and special characters may gain the ability to purchase a sixth dot in an Attribute\u201c, while p. 54 says \u201cAttributes are generally rated from 1-5. Some characters may have the ability to raise their normal maximum to 6, though this requires an Edge.\u201d<br /> <br /> AEon further complicates this on p.125 by saying (about Tier 3 characters) \u201cAll characters in this Tier share certain advantages. Instead of 8, their target number for all rolls is 7. In addition, they can possess up to six dots in any Attribute and can increase this to seven dots if they possess the Extraordinary Attribute Edge.\u201d Character Tier on p.71 and 74 of Core make no reference to higher Tier characters having a higher Attribute maximum as well.<br /> <br /> Edit to add: For clarity, AEon misnamed the Superior Trait Edge as Extraordinary Attribute.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-03T18:38:02-08:00","id":1278475,"title":"","content":"Page 157 lists one of the gifts the player purchased as \u201cSaw that Coming\u201d but that is not listed","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24935-werlynn","name":"werlynn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"192"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-04T06:44:09-08:00","id":1278563,"title":"","content":"Does repeating the dodge stunt against each of 5 attacks progressively build up my defense to silly levels or does each dodge replace the previous one? The former seems ridiculous. The later makes it so you could take a chance to get a better roll, but aren\u2019t encouraged to perform repetitive time burning rolls every time you\u2019re attacked like the stacking version. I\u2019m OK with rolling dodge once and it setting your defense for the rest of the round, but stacking a massive bonus seems clunky and disruptive to the system\u2019s otherwise reasonable difficulties and modifiers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24935-werlynn","name":"werlynn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"192"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-04T08:20:50-08:00","id":1278592,"title":"","content":"Breath Control:<br /> <br /> My understanding was that edges are not supernatural powers. Holding ones breath for 40 minutes seems supernatural. 8 x stamina minutes is nuts.<br /> <br /> I don\u2019t understand why the second part of the edge has you checking for suffocation every 8 or 4 minutes and removes the stamina component.<br /> <br /> It would be helpful if there were a place in the book where it actually covered suffocation and holding your breath, otherwise the description of this edge would be the only place to find base line breath hold time. I get that it\u2019s something to do with the indirect damage rules but those rules could use some samples such as drowning.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24935-werlynn","name":"werlynn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"192"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-04T09:05:33-08:00","id":1278608,"title":"","content":"page 8: &quot;<b>Oop</b>, hang on, big noise&quot; - Should be Oops I think<br /> page 28: In the red handwritten note one line ends with &quot;s&quot;, the next line begins with &quot;even&quot; - I think, the word seven should be reunited.<br /> page 35: The introductory text states that there are five steps during character creation, but the actual process involves six.<br /> page 36: A path can be a single word or a short phrase that summarizes the nature of character's experiences - missing <b>the</b> between of and character's<br /> page 37: Players should rank the three Arenas in order of <b>at</b> which their characters are most adept - should drop at<br /> page 38: Example: The Favored Approach should raise Cunning to four dots: Starts at one and gets two more dots allocated.<br /> page 39: The text refers to the Experience table below, but it is located above the text.<br /> page 43: Detective Example Connections: <b>New</b> Reporter should be News Reporter<br /> page 45: For example, <b>if</b> a character might - should drop if<br /> page 45: A Skill Ttrick that allows a character to increase her relative speed for action - missing <b>an</b> or <b>the</b><br /> page 112: In the sample combat, the henchmen have a Physical Arena of 4 at one point and 5 at another.<br /> page 115: Station: Contact Actions:<b>relying</b> crucial information should be relaying crucial information<br /> page 123: Example Weapons: the Katana lists both the Quality and the Quality 2 tag which seems redundant","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24456,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24456-xizzillix","user":"Xizzillix","date":". 01-09-2019, 09:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24456-xizzillix","name":"Xizzillix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-04T15:45:00-08:00","id":1278715,"title":"","content":"Combat - Dodge and Defense Stunts last until the end of the round, but combat resolution specifically calls for the defender to roll defense for each attack. I believe this is an error and the defender only rolls against the first attack and establishes defense against other attacks within the round from that roll. Requires clarification as some groups are reading it as defenders continue to roll against each attack, and their defense stacks higher and higher as the round progresses because defense specifically lingers until the end of the round.<br /> <br /> Edit: the Attack Resolution table on p.115 of Scion Origin indicates you only roll against the first attack, but this table isn\u2019t replicated in Core.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-05T02:19:17-08:00","id":1278795,"title":"","content":"p. 80: Moving and maneuvering<br /> The text in the first paragraph revers to &quot;range bands (p. XX)&quot;, but range bands seem not to be defined/explained anywhere, though this term is mentioned a lot in the Core and Aeon PDF. What is a range band? Examples:<br /> <br /> Aeon book, p. 196: &quot;This includes the same range band categories: close, short, medium, long, extreme, and out of range.&quot;<br /> So, the different ranges ARE the range bands?<br /> <br /> Aeon book, p. 256, Blink power: &quot;The character teleports no more than a single range band [...]&quot;<br /> I understand that ranges for psi powers are measured by psi, e.g. short for psi 2 and 3. Does this mean that the psion can teleport up to 1x short range (30m)?<br /> <br /> Core book, p. 196, Pretty damned fast gift: &quot;Additionally, she can move up to two range bands [...]&quot;<br /> Normally a human can move &quot;an unimpeded human on foot can move a number of meters each turn equal to twice their Athletics + highest Physical Attribute&quot; (core book, p. 80). How does this translate into a range band so that you can move even two of them as this gift allows?<br /> <br /> In general I find the whole range band stuff quite confusing when trying to measure how far a character can move.<br /> <br /> -------<br /> <br /> p. 79: &quot;Reflexive actions and movement up to her Stamina do not require [...]&quot;<br /> Better to write &quot;up to her Stamina <b>in meters</b> do not&quot;<br /> Also, why isn't this part written in the Moving and Maneuvering section (p. 80)? These details are spread over the book, making looking them up difficult.<br /> <br /> p. 102: &quot;Disarm&quot; stunt: It says &quot;range increment&quot;. Better to use the term &quot;range band&quot; here?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3122-shuragil","name":"shuragil","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-07T06:29:10-08:00","id":1279182,"title":"","content":"Some questions about paths:<br /> <br /> <br /> About assets:<br /> <br /> p. 40: &quot;The character does not have a connection to all of these groups; the player must choose one.&quot;<br /> So you have _one_ group connection (even if more than one are plausible for the path) per path<br /> <br /> What about assets (p.40)? Here no such restriction is mentioned. Does this mean that assets not chosen at path creation, made up on the fly during play with common sense? I mean, the finger print database example in the book is one of many possible accesses for a police chief path. Would sound a bit illogical if you'd have access to the finger print DB, but not to, say, the evidence room.<br /> <br /> <br /> Using up connections:<br /> <br /> p. 40: &quot;she may attempt to complete it to regain her connection rating after using her connections.&quot;<br /> It's not mentioned anywhere that connections have ratings (mentioned only for contacts). Also no mechanics are explained on how to expend these ratings. So it's confusing to find a sentence on how to _regain_ ratings.<br /> <br /> <br /> Path dots:<br /> <br /> I get it that a path begins with one dot:<br /> p. 40: &quot;Each Contact begins with one dot [...]&quot;<br /> p. 41: &quot;Initially, each connection has the same dot rating as the overall Path.&quot;<br /> Would be nice to explicitly state so.<br /> <br /> <br /> Edit: About connection groups:<br /> It's a bit strange that one path only grants connection to _one_ path related group. You can get connections to multiple contacts, so why not other ones as well?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3122,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3122-shuragil","user":"shuragil","date":". 01-07-2019, 09:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3122-shuragil","name":"shuragil","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-07T07:00:31-08:00","id":1279192,"title":"","content":"Skill specialties, p. 45:<br /> <br /> So a specialty in a skill (e.g. pistols for Aim) can only be used for OTHER skills as an enhancement? Not when shooting the bad guys using pistols?<br /> <br /> Also, a three-point enhancement as a free bonus when using pistols at Aim 5? Wow, though admittetly I didn't playtest yet, so don't really know if this is too high or not.<br /> <br /> Also see this thread for more skill specialy questions:<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1274245-are-specialties-improperly-defined\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1274245-are-specialties-improperly-defined\"> Are specialties improperly defined? - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1274245-are-specialties-improperly-defined\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1274245-are-specialties-improperly-defined </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> p.45 (core) Specialties says that having a specialty in a skill provides enhancement towards OTHER skills when relevant. However, p.52 - Pilot - I can figure it out, p.84 Hacking and p.91 Crafting all seem to imply that a specialty is necessary to perform specific functions with a skill. I can figure it out implies that pilot requires specific specialties for specific types of vehicles Hacking states dice pool of enigmas + cunning and a specialty of Cryptography or Software is required. Cryptography seems like it should be an enigmas specialty and Software should be a technology specialty. How </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3122-shuragil","name":"shuragil","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-07T07:08:30-08:00","id":1279195,"title":"","content":"Initiative, p. 79:<br /> &quot;Each player rolls, as well as the Storyguide for Storyguide Characters.&quot;<br /> Rolls what? The answer is found elsewhere, p. 99: &quot;Each player rolls the lower of Athletics + Cunning or Empathy + Dexterity.&quot;<br /> <br /> When looking up the initiative rolls in the table of contents I get p. 79 for initiative and don't find the requested information. This is another example of what I meant when I said in another thread the information is spread through the book, making looking up things unnecessarily frustrating.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3122-shuragil","name":"shuragil","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-07T07:23:16-08:00","id":1279202,"title":"","content":"Artifact edge:<br /> <br /> In the core book, p. 65: Can the &quot;Artifact&quot; edge only be taken by Talent characters? What if my psion wants his own spaceship or so? Is there some kind of edge similar to the old 1e background &quot;Device&quot; which can take care of this? Would this edge cost be similar to that of the old background?<br /> <br /> What if my character wants to have an item which is not super-science, but some kind regular, but too-expensive (not possible with the wealth edge), item, like a tank, mentioned starship, a big yacht or mansion etc.? Can this be covered with the Artifact edge as well? How?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3122-shuragil","name":"shuragil","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-07T18:04:15-08:00","id":1279352,"title":"","content":"When rolling to resist indirect damage the difficulty is 1. According to the rules, only additional successes reduce the damage. What do you gain for succeeding at the roll?<br /> <br /> I\u2019ve seen this in a few spots\u2014in particular in Psi powers. Please make sure that any check in this system that meets the set difficulty has the intended effect. If that means raising difficulties then do that, but make sure that success is success.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24935-werlynn","name":"werlynn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"192"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-08T02:23:40-08:00","id":1279433,"title":"","content":"Edge &quot;Adrenalin Spike&quot;, p. 59:<br /> &quot;She can ignore an Injury Complication one time per day [...]&quot;<br /> Ignore for one single roll? For a single round? Something else?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3122-shuragil","name":"shuragil","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-08T13:50:08-08:00","id":1279558,"title":"","content":"Page 180 lists Safe House as a Les Fantomes Edge, but as far as I can find no such Edge is found in the book.<br /> <br /> Edit: LRE also has it listed as one of their Edges on page 178.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 01-08-2019, 04:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-09T14:59:51-08:00","id":1279786,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1273286-trinity-continuum-core-errata?p=1279558#post1279558\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Page 180 lists Safe House as a Les Fantomes Edge, but as far as I can find no such Edge is found in the book.<br /> <br /> Edit: LRE also has it listed as one of their Edges on page 178.</div> </div> </div> </div>It\u2019s in \u00c6on under the Nor\u00e7a","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24935-werlynn","name":"werlynn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"192"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-09T17:42:43-08:00","id":1279819,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>werlynn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1273286-trinity-continuum-core-errata?p=1279786#post1279786\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It\u2019s in \u00c6on under the Nor\u00e7a</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Probably not the best place for a corebook edge.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/453-megazarak","name":"MegaZarak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar453_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-10T13:22:48-08:00","id":1279956,"title":"","content":"Page 51: The last sentence of Walking Wounded appears to be missing some words between 'Trick,' and 'act', &quot;After being treated with this Skill <b><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trick, act</span></b> without any penalty from that injury.&quot; Perhaps something like, 'the treated character' <br /> <br /> Page 60: The prerequisite for Alternate Identity is &quot;Appropriate Path for Alternate Identity **&quot; How do we determine what is an appropriate Path for Alternate Identity 2?<br /> <br /> Page 63: The First sentence of Forceful Martial Arts should have <span style=\"color:#0000FF\">clubs </span>instead of <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">cubs</span>. &quot;...hand to hand weapons, like chain weapons, <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b>cubs</b></span>, fists...&quot;<br /> <br /> Page 63: The second sentence of the two-dot ability of Forceful Martial Arts, Deadly Strike, contains an extraneous <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">for</span>. &quot;...whenever she uses <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b>for </b></span>this attack.<br /> <br /> Page 75: The paragraph describing the two ways time is measured reads weird to me. I am finding it hard to articulate what I am feeling here so I may come back and edit this post for this spot.<br /> <br /> Page 81: The last sentence of the DROP PRONE/STAND section appears to be missing a '<span style=\"color:#0000FF\">from</span>' at the end of the sentence. &quot;A prone character's Defense changes depending on where her enemies are attacking her. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23768-graywulfe","name":"graywulfe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23768_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-10T17:04:28-08:00","id":1279998,"title":"","content":"p 76, 1st bullet &quot;<b>Session: </b>The encompasses...&quot;<br /> Should probably read as either, &quot;Session: The session encompasses...&quot; or &quot;Session: Encompasses....&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23804-uri-meca","name":"Uri Meca","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-11T12:38:29-08:00","id":1280158,"title":"","content":"Page 150 of the Trinity Core states that once per scene a Talent may add a Facet\u2019s rating as an Enhancement to a roll if it fits the Facet. No cost is mentioned.<br /> <br /> The next page, listing things one spends inspiration for describes doing that in three separate entries, one for each Facet. No limit on uses per scene is mentioned.<br /> <br /> <br /> It is unclear whether the latter is a clarification of how the former works (in which case the former\u2019s mention of \u201conce per scene\u201d and the latter\u2019s exclusion of it is very confusing), if these are meant as two separate rules (so you can do it once per scene for free, but it costs Inspiration to do it more), or if one of the two is a relic of a defunct rule .","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 01-11-2019, 06:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}